{"id": "ebf6f512-ac58-47fc-b90a-487795e3ad70", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The user has a specific hypothesis already—EBS burst balance on a burstable instance—so this seems like a bounded troubleshooting task: check instance and volume metrics to confirm or rule it out. It's potentially delegatable since it involves token-heavy metric review rather than open-ended root-cause analysis.

I'm thinking I should send a brief message outlining the plan, then dispatch a single subagent to pull CloudWatch metrics for the instance and volume. Since region isn't specified, I'll have it default to us-east-1 and search across regions/accounts if needed, focusing on the 18:30-19:03Z window compared against an earlier baseline.

"}]}

{"id": "ee74ffce-c4ac-41fd-9676-71126c6fc5b9", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check the instance and volume metrics to confirm the I/O burst-balance drain and see what's driving it. That means looking at EBS bandwidth and IOPS against the instance's limits.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_8QxfilVq1HoblF6ULnU1kj", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "ebs-burst-check", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "investigating-infrastructure-changes"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Confirm and quantify why the application on EC2 instance i-0123456789abcdef0_1 became slow in the last ~30 minutes. Hypothesis from the user: the instance is burstable, its gp3 volume vol-0123456789abcdef0 is provisioned with more IOPS/throughput than the instance's EBS limits can deliver, and EBSIOBalance% is draining so the instance is being throttled at its baseline EBS performance.",
  "context": "Shallow first pass. Locate the instance (agent space account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1 first; if not found, check other associated accounts/regions). Determine instance type and its EBS baseline vs. burst IOPS/throughput (use describe_instance_types EbsInfo), the volume's provisioned IOPS/throughput/size, and whether the volume is attached to this instance.",
  "resources": ["i-0123456789abcdef0_1", "vol-0123456789abcdef0"],
  "timeframe": "Incident window 2026-11-11T18:30:00Z to 2026-11-11T19:03:00Z; baseline: preceding 3-6 hours (e.g. 2026-11-11T13:00:00Z to 2026-11-11T18:30:00Z)",
  "criteria": "Report: (1) EBSIOBalance% and EBSByteBalance% trend (when did it start draining, current value, whether it hit 0); (2) actual volume IOPS and throughput (VolumeReadOps/WriteOps, VolumeReadBytes/WriteBytes) vs. the instance's baseline and burst EBS limits and vs. the volume's provisioned values; (3) VolumeQueueLength, VolumeIdleTime, VolumeTotalReadTime/WriteTime latency, and instance-level EBSReadOps/EBSWriteOps, EBSReadBytes/EBSWriteBytes; (4) CPUUtilization/CPUCreditBalance to rule out CPU credit exhaustion as a concurrent cause; (5) what changed in the workload at onset (I/O load increase, recent config/volume modification or deployment) if easily visible. Conclude whether instance-level EBS throttling explains the slowness, and suggest remediation options (larger/non-burstable instance type, reduce provisioned IOPS/throughput, reduce I/O load). Keep it concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check EBS burst balance and I/O metrics for the instance"}], "created_at": null}

